{
  "_comment": [
    "The S1 starting-path run fixture (T-082). This file is the run's ground truth: the",
    "roster it solicits and the counts the flow is graded against. Trust SCORES are not here",
    "on purpose: the snapshot the ranker filters on is built by trust.snapshot.build_snapshot",
    "from the seeded blacklist, so the blacklist flag is the trust engine's answer and not a",
    "row this fixture wrote.",
    "",
    "The catalogue each hosted store's agent reads lives here too, and",
    "`bid_placed == n_stores_solicited` is checked against",
    "`expected.solicited` here, so a silent drop in solicitation cannot pass by agreeing with",
    "itself.",
    "",
    "Roles are the four the starting path has to distinguish: two hosted stores whose agents",
    "really answer, one store that never answers (so the exchange represents it at list price",
    "- R10's fallback), and one blacklisted store that must never be solicited, ranked, shown",
    "or accepted anywhere in the run (S8 release blocker)."
  ],
